# Code owners (plan M4c decision 4). The revocation path is under the two-person rule (design contract 10): every
# change needs the review of the revocation reviewers, and the branch protection of main requires two approving
# reviews from code owners for these paths. Add the second reviewer here, and move to a team when the repository moves
# to an organization.
/agent/internal/revoke/     @phischl
/agent/cmd/paddock-revoke/  @phischl
# The crypttab volume selection paddock-revoke erases (shared with the luks reconciler, PDK-009).
/agent/internal/luks/crypttab.go  @phischl
# The secret scan (PDK-065): CI reads its configuration from a pull request's merge base, but a pull request runs its
# own workflows, Makefile and scripts, so the scan's integrity rests on the review of these paths. GitHub enforces
# these owners only once branch protection requires code-owner review (docs/operations/secret-scan.md).
/.gitleaks.toml           @phischl
/.gitleaksignore          @phischl
/Makefile                 @phischl
/.github/                 @phischl
/deploy/compose/scripts/  @phischl
